### Privacy lab: API client for the live demo (IntelliJ HTTP Client). Requests go through the gateway.
### Synthetic accounts from V2__seed_demo_users.sql: alice=1, bob=2, dpo=3, marketing=4, erin=5
### (ids after `./scripts/privacy-demo.sh reset`).

@gw = http://localhost:8080

### Step 1 - registration: e-mail, phone, password, verification token (check `docker logs plantshop-user-service`)
POST {{gw}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: demo-step1-http-client

{
  "fullName": "Log Demo",
  "email": "log.demo.{{$random.alphanumeric(6)}}@example.test",
  "phone": "+44 7700 900999",
  "password": "Demo-Passw0rd-2026"
}

### Step 1 - password reset: one-time reset token (same answer for unknown accounts)
POST {{gw}}/api/users/password-reset
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: demo-step1-http-client

{ "email": "alice@example.test" }

### Step 2 - Alice exports her own data
GET {{gw}}/api/users/1/personal-data
Authorization: Basic alice@example.test Alice-Demo-2026

### Step 2 - negative: Bob asks for Alice's data -> 404, same as for a missing profile
GET {{gw}}/api/users/1/personal-data
Authorization: Basic bob@example.test Bob-Demo-2026

### Step 2 - negative: a profile that does not exist -> identical 404
GET {{gw}}/api/users/999999/personal-data
Authorization: Basic bob@example.test Bob-Demo-2026

### Step 2 - privacy officer exports on the customer's behalf
GET {{gw}}/api/users/1/personal-data
Authorization: Basic dpo@example.test Dpo-Demo-2026

### Step 3 - erasure by Erin herself (POST only)
POST {{gw}}/api/users/5/anonymize
Authorization: Basic erin@example.test Erin-Demo-2026

### Step 3 - repeat by the privacy officer -> ALREADY_ANONYMIZED, nothing changes
POST {{gw}}/api/users/5/anonymize
Authorization: Basic dpo@example.test Dpo-Demo-2026

### Step 3 - negative: Bob tries to erase Alice -> 404
POST {{gw}}/api/users/1/anonymize
Authorization: Basic bob@example.test Bob-Demo-2026

### Step 4 - Alice's consents and their history
GET {{gw}}/api/users/1/consents
Authorization: Basic alice@example.test Alice-Demo-2026

### Step 4 - campaign e-mail to Alice (marketing operator): DENY before consent / after revoke, ALLOW after grant
POST {{gw}}/api/marketing/emails
Authorization: Basic marketing@example.test Marketing-Demo-2026
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": 1, "campaign": "autumn-sale" }

### Step 4 - GRANT marketing e-mails (current policy version)
POST {{gw}}/api/users/1/consents/MARKETING_EMAIL/grant
Authorization: Basic alice@example.test Alice-Demo-2026
Content-Type: application/json

{ "policyVersion": "marketing-v2", "source": "WEB" }

### Step 4 - REVOKE marketing e-mails
POST {{gw}}/api/users/1/consents/MARKETING_EMAIL/revoke
Authorization: Basic alice@example.test Alice-Demo-2026
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "WEB" }

### Step 4 - optional analytics of the signed-in customer (needs OPTIONAL_ANALYTICS consent)
POST {{gw}}/api/analytics/events
Authorization: Basic alice@example.test Alice-Demo-2026
Content-Type: application/json

{ "event": "plant_viewed", "page": "/plants/3" }
